WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.370
These days, it feels like just about everyone
is in love with the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:10.289
But even though plenty of big name, Oscar-caliber
stars have signed on to the MCU, there are

00:00:10.289 --> 00:00:14.900
some actors who aren't so enamored with Marvel
movies, and aren't afraid to say so. Here's

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:18.980
a look at some big name actors who have criticized
the MCU.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:19.980
Simon Pegg

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:26.250
In 2015, Simon Pegg bit that hand that feeds
him by trashing science fiction and comic

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:31.500
book movies, saying society was being, quote,
"infantilized" by superhero movies and that

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.239
they're, quote, "taking our focus away from
real-world issues."

00:00:35.239 --> 00:00:39.829
Pegg called out Avengers: Age of Ultron specifically,
saying that films used to give us

00:00:39.829 --> 00:00:44.149
"challenging, emotional journeys [...] Now
we're walking out of the cinema really not

00:00:44.149 --> 00:00:48.450
thinking about anything, other than the fact
that the Hulk had a fight with a robot."

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:52.870
Unsurprisingly, Pegg also had a bone to pick
with Marvel Studios over how they treated

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:56.690
his pal Edgar Wright, saying that Wright's
original Ant-Man script was

00:00:56.690 --> 00:01:01.750
"Daring, fun, and hugely exciting. Shame we
won't see it."

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:03.600
Jodie Foster

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:08.210
The Avengers and their ilk may save the world
on the screen, but according to Jodie Foster,

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:13.970
when it comes to the hearts and minds of audiences,
they do the exact opposite. Foster told Radio

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:19.750
Times she had no interest in directing superhero
movies, and she compared Marvel and DC's films

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:22.580
to literally harming the planet. She said:

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:28.270
"Studios making bad content in order to appeal
to the masses and shareholders is like fracking,

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:32.369
you get the best return right now but you
wreck the earth. […] It's ruining the viewing

00:01:32.369 --> 00:01:36.310
habits of the American population and ultimately
the rest of the world."

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:40.860
Guardians of the Galaxy writer and director
James Gunn responded on Twitter, saying,

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:46.609
"I think Foster looks at film in an old-fashioned
way where spectacle film can’t be thought-provoking.

00:01:46.609 --> 00:01:50.780
[…] Creating spectacle films that are innovative,
humane, and thoughtful is what excites me

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:52.909
about this job."

00:01:52.909 --> 00:01:54.530
George Takei

00:01:54.530 --> 00:02:00.310
In 2016, when Tilda Swinton was cast as Stephen
Strange's mentor the Ancient One in Marvel's

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:05.100
Doctor Strange, critics accused Marvel of
whitewashing. Doctor Strange co-writer C.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:09.800
Robert Cargill responded by claiming they
made the character Celtic instead of Tibetan

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:12.700
in order to avoid angering Chinese censors.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:17.450
That didn't sit well with Star Trek icon George
Takei, who posted on Facebook

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:23.010
"You cast a white actress so you wouldn’t
hurt sales…in Asia? This backpedaling is

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:27.310
nearly as cringeworthy as the casting. Marvel
must think we’re all idiots.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:31.970
He went on to point out that they moved the
Ancient One's headquarters from Tibet to Nepal

00:02:31.970 --> 00:02:35.060
anyway, which should have taken care of the
issue to begin with.

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:38.360
"It wouldn't have mattered to the Chinese
government by that point whether the character

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:42.340
was white or Asian. It was already in another
country."

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:44.330
Jessica Chastain

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:49.110
In August 2014, while speaking to TheWrap
about women having difficulty finding good

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:53.870
roles in Hollywood, Jessica Chastain singled
out Scarlett Johansson's Black Widow as an

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:58.340
example of a powerful female character and
said the fact that Marvel hadn't made a solo

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:00.340
Black Widow movie made no sense.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:05.370
"I don't understand it, why is it taking so
long for this? To me, it's a no-brainer. You

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:08.760
want to make money, put Scarlett Johansson
in a superhero movie!"

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:13.370
There's some good news, though: after the
success of 2017's Wonder Woman, Marvel finally

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:17.550
began listening, and a Black Widow film is
currently in development.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:19.180
Chloe Bennet

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:23.680
You wouldn't think someone currently working
for Marvel would take potshots at them, but

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:29.210
Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. star Chloe Bennet did
just that in 2016 when she expressed frustration

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:33.370
with her show consistently being ignored by
the movies even though they take place in

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:37.130
the same shared universe. She told a crowd
of fans at a comic book convention,

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:41.300
"People who make movies for Marvel, why don't
you acknowledge what happens on our show?

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:45.060
Why don't you guys go ask them that? 'Cause
they don't seem to care! […]I am kind of,

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:49.170
like, ready for Steve Rogers to make an appearance
on our show. I'd be okay with that. And like,

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:51.980
where's Romanoff? Where's the Avengers?"

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:53.170
Christopher Eccleston

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:58.940
Thor: The Dark World star Christopher Eccleston
is another onetime Marvel employee who wasn't

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:03.290
quite so happy with the studio, not because
they didn't give his character enough attention,

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:08.420
but because they gave him way too much. Eccleston
told Graham Norton that in order to play the

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:13.760
evil Malekith, Eccleston had to endure several
hours in makeup every day, something he says

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:15.790
Marvel hid from him when he signed on.

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:19.600
"Marvel were dishonest to me. Because they
never, ever let me know that there'd be that

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:20.660
amount of make-up."

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:24.730
And he was even more direct when speaking
to The Guardian about the experience.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.750
"Thor? Just a gun in your mouth."

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:31.790
So, y'know, don't count on Malekith coming
back to pester Thor anytime soon.

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:33.640
Mel Gibson

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.480
Considering Mel Gibson once said of a critic

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:39.900
"I want to kill him. I want his intestines
on a stick. I want to kill his dog,"

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:43.810
you have to take it seriously when he starts
complaining about excess violence.

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:48.010
Calling superhero films "violence without
conscience" in an interview with the Washington

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:53.120
Post, he contrasted his approach to the 2016
drama Hacksaw Ridge with Marvel's output.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:56.910
"Look at any Marvel movie. They’re more
violent than anything that I’ve done, but

00:04:56.910 --> 00:05:01.020
[in my movies,] you give a s*** about the
characters, which makes it matter more. That’s

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:02.450
all I’ll say."

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:04.010
Jason Momoa

00:05:04.010 --> 00:05:09.480
Even before Jason Momoa made his debut as
Aquaman in the DC Extended Universe, the star,

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:15.150
at a fan's request, personalized an autographed
photo with "F*** Marvel" at the Indiana Comic-Con.

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:19.930
The photo, and particularly the offending
phrase, traveled quickly across the web feeding

00:05:19.930 --> 00:05:22.670
fuel to the decades-old Marvel/DC rivalry.

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:27.880
To his credit, Momoa wasn't too pleased about
the autograph going viral, explaining at Pureto

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:31.110
Rico Comic Con that it was just a joke that
got blown way out of proportion.

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:33.310
"I love X-Men, I grew up, I love Wolverine.
My kids love Spider-Man. It's just silly.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:41.190
I'll leave my sense of humor at the bottom
of the ocean next time."

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:45.540
Thanks for watching! Click the Looper icon
to subscribe to our YouTube channel. Plus

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.750
check out all this cool stuff we know you'll
love, too!

